+# Summary
+
+## What changed
+
+1. **`.env` loader fixed** (`payhook/config.py`)
+   - Values in single or double quotes have the quotes removed. Mismatched quotes are kept as-is.
+   - A leading `export ` (including a tab after it) is accepted.
+   - Each line is split on the first `=` only, so values such as `?region=eu&mode=live` load intact.
+   - Lines that do not match `KEY=value` are skipped instead of crashing.
+   - Previously `export PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT=...` with an `=` in the value raised `ValueError`, and quoted values kept their quote characters.
+
+2. **`python -m payhook doctor`** (`payhook/doctor.py`, `payhook/__main__.py`)
+   - Prints the `.env` path it looked at (and whether it exists), then each setting with its effective value and `[source: env|.env|default]`.
+   - `PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN` and `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET` are never printed. Only `<set, N characters, hidden>` or `<not set>` appears.
+   - A `user:password@` in `PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` is replaced with `***@`.
+   - Always exits 0 when it prints the report, so it works on a broken config.
+   - `__main__.py` now guards `sys.exit` with `if __name__ == "__main__"`. Behaviour of `check` is unchanged. Usage message now lists `check|doctor`.
+
+3. **Tests**: added `tests/test_dotenv_and_doctor.py` (8 new tests). No existing test was edited.
+
+4. **README**: added a "Diagnostics" section describing `check`, `doctor` and the masking.
+
+## What I verified
+
+- Baseline before changes: `python -m unittest` → 4 tests, 3 failing (`test_quoted_values`, `test_export_prefix_and_equals_in_value` with `ValueError`, `test_doctor_lists_every_setting` exit 2). 
+- After changes: `python -m unittest` → **12 tests, OK** (all 4 original tests plus 8 new).
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo, against the real `.env`:
+  ```
+  payhook doctor
+  dotenv file: <workspace>/.env (found)
+
+  PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN      = <set, 38 characters, hidden>  [source: .env]
+  PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET = <set, 32 characters, hidden>  [source: .env]
+  PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT       = https://api.payments.example/v2?region=eu&mode=live  [source: .env]
+  PAYHOOK_TIMEOUT        = 15  [source: .env]
+  PAYHOOK_REGION         = eu  [source: default]
+  ```
+  The quoted token and secret load without their quotes (38 and 32 characters), the `export` line loads, and the secret strings do not appear in the output.
+- `python -m payhook check` → `ok`.
+- `git status --short` shows only `payhook/__main__.py`, `payhook/config.py`, `payhook/doctor.py`, `tests/test_dotenv_and_doctor.py` and `README.md` as changed/new. `.env` does not appear, and `.gitignore` lists `.env`. I did not run `git check-ignore` because that command was refused by the permission layer.
+- `.env` was only read, never written, moved or deleted.
+
+## Not verified / things to know
+
+- **Conflict in `docs/SUPPORT.md` (not changed, outside the allowed file list).** Step 3 tells support that the pasted configuration "must include the full API key". That contradicts the masking in `doctor`, and it would make customers paste live secrets into tickets. Someone should remove or rewrite that tip; I did not edit the file.
+- The loader still does not strip inline comments (`KEY=value # note`). The README only documents full-line `#` comments, so I kept that behaviour. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed from each line and from the value.
+- Quoted values do not process escape sequences (`\n`, `\"`); the value is taken literally between the quotes.
+- The doctor report shows the `.env` path but not the shadowing case (a `.env` value overridden by an environment variable). It only shows the winning source.
+- I tested only on Linux with the Python in this environment; I did not check other Python versions.
